The Go rendering: an application whose packages hold assembly, C and object
files. Package asm's amd64 assembly reads a constant through go_asm.h as an
operand and in an #ifdef, a variable, a struct field offset and a constant it
stores through a pointer, and calls a Go function; one iota group of it is
named in Go only by its first member. Package arch's helper is called only from
s390x assembly, which no corpus host builds. Package b's amd64 assembly is only
an #include of a file whose name starts with an underscore, which loads an
unexported variable of package a, and its s390x assembly calls a function of
package a. Package a2, which the command imports for its effects, holds only an
underscore-named assembly fragment. Package
cpart imports "C", compiles a C file and exports a hook. Package sysopart holds
an object file for s390x.

